# Build-context excludes for examples/reference-app/Dockerfile, whose build
# context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (not examples/reference-app/) -- the
# Dockerfile's own header comment explains why: this app's go.mod replace
# directives point at sibling go/* modules by relative path, and it builds
# under go.work workspace mode, so the build stage needs go.work,
# go.work.sum and every one of go.work's `use` entries -- the go/* modules,
# tools/configrefgen and examples/reference-app -- all visible in one
# context.
#
# This file follows .gitignore's own patterns rather than duplicating its
# reasoning (see that file for the comments this one deliberately omits);
# it adds a few entries .gitignore has no reason to carry (docs/site's own
# build output, the two web node_modules trees) purely because a
# COMMITTED file can never bloat the git-tracked tree the way an untracked
# build artifact can bloat a naively-sent Docker build context.

# Version control and agent tooling -- never needed inside a build context.
.git/
.claude/

# IDE and OS cruft (.gitignore's own entries).
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment files -- may hold real local secrets; never sent to the
# daemon, and never needed by the Dockerfile's own COPY list either.
.env
.env.local
*.local

# Go build artifacts (.gitignore's own entries) -- test binaries and
# coverage output, never build inputs.
**/*.test
*.out
go/**/bin/

# Python tooling caches (.gitignore's own entries).
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node -- both pnpm workspaces (web/ and examples/reference-app/web, an
# external member of the same workspace) can carry a node_modules tree
# large enough on its own to dwarf the rest of this repository, and the
# Dockerfile's backend build needs neither: it never touches web/ or
# examples/reference-app/web at all.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The merged OpenAPI document now lives at contracts/speed.yaml, a
# committed file that needs no exclusion here -- a committed file can
# never bloat the Docker build context the way an untracked build
# artifact can, and the Go build this Dockerfile runs never reads it.
/tmp/

# Local SQLite data (.gitignore's own entries) -- a stray reference-app.db
# from local development must never ride along into the image or even the
# build context.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite

# Hugo's generated docs-site output and build lock (.gitignore's own
# entries) -- can be large once built, and the Dockerfile never reads
# docs/ at all.
docs/site/public/
docs/site/resources/
docs/site/.hugo_build.lock

# This file and the Dockerfile it configures are the two build-context
# inputs docker itself always needs regardless of ignore rules, so neither
# is listed here to exclude.
